            <div xml:id="d658">

                <pb facs="0669" n="569" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg569"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72114/5415: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-25T09:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">May 25, 1920—9
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:34 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>170. From Winterburn for A[djutant] G[eneral], War [Department].</p>
                <p>“Number 31, May 24th. For Hines. <hi rendition="#italic">Sherman</hi> arrived May
                    22nd sailed to-day for Trieste, first stop Singapore, with 134 first, 70 second,
                    1787 troops, total 1991 Czecho-Slovak troops. About 13,200 Czechs remain to be
                    repatriated on transports <hi rendition="#italic">Eidellyn, Madcuwuska,
                        Sheridan, Heffron, America</hi>. All Czecho-Slovak troops now in
                    Vladivostok.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
